 "0", "4508": "1", "4525": "0", "453": "0", "4531": "0", "4554": "0", "4580": "1", "4585": "1", "4662": "1", "4668": "0", "4677": "0", "4704": "0", "4771": "1", "4774": "1", "4778": "1", "490": "0", "50": "0", "57": "0", "570": "0", "573": "1", "590": "1", "595": "0", "597": "0", "630": "0", "648": "0", "656": "0", "685": "0", "714": "1", "718": "1", "721": "0", "744": "0", "773": "0", "793": "1", "794": "1", "795": "1", "805": "1", "817": "0", "850": "0", "871": "0", "873": "1", "89": "1", "918": "0", "925": "0", "928": "1", "952": "0", "964": "0", "967": "1"}, "codebook": {"decision_rules": [{"negative_example": {"explanation": "The senator introduces legislation and states policy goals, but no concrete outcome, funded resource, designation, or adoption is attributed to the senator's action. Introducing or supporting a bill without a resulting claimed accomplishment is not credit-claiming.", "text": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Washington D C Today Senator Edward M Kennedy introduced legislation to enhance stem cell research and to strengthen anti cloning provisions Kennedy joined by his colleagues and co sponsors of the Human Cloning Ban and Stem Cell Research Protection Act highlighted the key provisions that separate this bill from similar pieces of legislation currently before Congress"}, "positive_example": {"explanation": "The senator explicitly announces that a local entity has received a specific federal grant and claims personal authorship and funding of the program that produced it. This is a direct claim of delivering federal resources to the state.", "text": "PARMA RECEIVES FIREFIGHTING GRANT THROUGH SEN. DEWINE'S BILL Sen. Mike DeWine (R-OH) today announced that the Parma Fire Department will receive $105,550 as part of his Firefighter Investment and Response Enhancement (FIRE) Act... Senator DeWine wrote and passed the FIRE Act (S. 1941) in 2000, establishing a grant program dedicated to providing federal assistance to local fire departments."}, "rule": "The text announces or publicizes federal funds, grants, projects, programs, facilities, designations, appointments, or other concrete resources or benefits secured, obtained, delivered, obtained approval for, or directed to the senator's state, localities, institutions, or constituents, and attributes the achievement to the senator's action, advocacy, request, work, or position."
  , "rule_id":   	"1"}, 
  {"negative_example": {"explanation": "This is a hearing statement about pending legislation. It discusses progress and goals, but does not claim enactment, passage, or inclusion of a specific senator-attributed accomplishment sufficient to meet the rule.", "text": "Statement Of Senator Patrick Leahy Hearing On The Fairness In Absestos Injury Resolution Act ... We must see our efforts through until we have a balanced and effective national trust fund that fairly compensates victims of asbestos related disease"}, "positive_example": {"explanation": "The text states the senator's amendment passed on a recorded bipartisan vote and frames the outcome as a victory produced by his legislative action. This is claiming a successful legislative result.", "text": "PRESS RELEASE SENATE ADOPTS NELSON AMENDMENT TO PROVIDE FAIRNESS FOR U S CATTLE PRODUCERS ... Nebraska s Senator Ben Nelson today said he was gratified that his amendment to prevent the USDA from allowing some Japanese beef imports back into the U S until the Japanese government also allows American beef to again be imported into Japan passed on a bipartisan vote of 72 to 26"}, "rule": "The text claims a successful legislative or congressional outcome—such as a bill, amendment, provision, resolution, or nomination being passed, approved, adopted, confirmed, enacted, signed, or included in final legislation—and attributes that outcome, or a material part of it, to the senator's authorship, sponsorship, amendment, vote, negotiation, or leadership.", "rule_id": "2"}, {"negative_example": {"explanation": "The senator announces legislation he introduced, but it has not yet passed or been enacted. Announcing or supporting pending legislation, without claiming success or delivery, is not credit-claiming.", "text": "SEN. WHITEHOUSE SPONSORS GLOBAL WARMING BILL AIMED AT WILDLIFE PROTECTION Calling global warming the single greatest threat to the world's natural environment, U.S. Senator Sheldon Whitehouse (D-R.I.) today announced new legislation calling for a national strategy to address the threat of climate change to America's wildlife."}, "positive_example": {"explanation": "The senator claims to have secured inclusion of specific dollar amounts in a spending bill and characterizes them as promises kept. This is claiming delivery of resources through the appropriations process.", "text": "SEN. MIKULSKI DELIVERS ON COMMITMENT TO BRAC-RELATED TRANSPORTATION PROJECTS ... today announced she has fought to include funding in the 2008 spending bill for key Maryland transportation projects, fulfilling her promise to help communities manage growth related to the 2005 Base Realignment and Closure (BRAC) Commission's recommendations. \"My promises made to BRAC-impacted communities are promises kept.\""}, "rule": "The text claims credit for obtaining or preserving a tangible benefit for the state or constituents through appropriations, earmarks, budget provisions, disaster declarations, regulatory decisions, agency actions, or administrative relief, where the senator claims to have obtained, protected, expedited, restored, or prevented loss of the benefit.", "rule_id": "3"}, {"negative_example": {"explanation": "The senator presents an award to community members. This honors others rather than claiming personal credit for securing a governmental benefit or accomplishment.", "text": "EVANSVILLE SCHOOL COMMUNITY COUNCIL'S TEAM RECEIVES LUGAR HEALTH AND FITNESS AWARD On Saturday, September 16, Sen. Dick Lugar honored the Evansville School Community Council's \"Nutrition and Physical Activities Team\" for its commitment to youth health and fitness."}, "positive_example": {"explanation": "The text presents an award based on the senator's votes and quotes the senator saying he was proud to side with taxpayers, thereby claiming a voting record as an accomplishment.", "text": "Alexander Named Hero of the Taxpayer Americans for Tax Reform Recognize Alexander with Award Based on Key Votes in 2005 ... U S Senator Lamar Alexander R TN has been named a Hero of the Taxpayer by Americans for Tax Reform ... I was proud to side with taxpayers on key votes before the U S Senate"}, "rule": "The text claims credit for the senator's past votes, awards, ratings, or recognitions tied directly to official actions, where the senator or the release uses the award or record to demonstrate personal accomplishment rather than merely reporting a ceremonial or honorary event.", "rule_id": "4"}, {"negative_example": {"explanation": "This is a statement of frustration and support for a bill that has not passed. It does not claim that the senator secured, passed, or delivered a concrete result.", "text": "Lieberman Frustrated By House Refusal to Take Up D C Voting Rights Bill ... said Wednesday the decision by House leaders not to call up a bipartisan District of Columbia voting rights bill during the lame duck session was extremely frustrating"}, "positive_example": {"explanation": "The release states the senators delivered on a promise to secure funding, identifies the specific amount and projects, and quotes local officials thanking the senators for their support and leadership. This is credit for obtaining federal resources.", "text": "SENS. BAUCUS, TESTER ANNOUNCE MORE THAN $12M FOR BUTTE Montana Senators Max Baucus and Jon Tester have delivered on their promise to secure federal funding for the Mining City. The Senators announced today that $12.5 million for vital military projects in Butte has been included in the Defense Appropriations Bill"}, "rule": "The text explicitly uses credit-claiming language—such as 'secured,' 'delivered,' 'obtained,' 'won,' 'brought home,' 'fought for and included,' 'helped get,' 'worked with officials to expedite approval,' or 'kept/protected'—to link the senator personally to a completed or officially announced benefit, even if the ultimate decision was made by an agency, department, or another governmental actor.", "rule_id": "5"}], "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator presents himself or herself as personally responsible for, instrumental in, or deserving recognition for producing a concrete benefit, resource, policy outcome, official action, or achievement for the state, constituents, institutions, or a policy area. The claim may be direct or implied, but it must connect the senator's action, position, advocacy, vote, or office to an obtained or successfully advanced result. Merely stating a policy position, introducing or cosponsoring legislation without claiming success, criticizing opponents or the administration, announcing meetings or events, offering condolences, or describing ongoing work without a claimed accomplishment is not credit-claiming."}}
